turns.text:
Minimal fix:

```js
const payload = jwt.decode(token);

if (!payload?.exp || Date.now() >= payload.exp * 1000) {
  return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token expired' });
}
```

`payload.exp` is in seconds; `Date.now()` is milliseconds, so multiply `exp` by `1000`.

Safer library-based alternative:

```js
try {
  const payload = jwt.verify(token, JWT_SECRET);
  req.user = payload;
  next();
} catch (err) {
  if (err.name === 'TokenExpiredError') {
    return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token expired' });
  }

  return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Invalid token' });
}
```

This is safer because `jwt.verify()` checks signature, expiration, and token validity together, instead of relying on `decode()` plus manual checks.

